  "aiContextParagraph": "Following the latest Israeli elections, former military head Gadi Eisenkot has been formally tasked with forming a new government. This mandate, issued by the Israeli presidency, provides the political newcomer with a period of up to six weeks to assemble a workable coalition. If he is unable to secure a majority within this timeframe, the mandate to form a cabinet is expected to return to caretaker Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu. Reports indicate that Eisenkot is currently pursuing outreach efforts toward various political factions, including allies of the outgoing prime minister. The process is being closely monitored by international observers, as the outcome remains uncertain regarding potential government structures and the future political role of the existing administration. The appointment follows a period of electoral activity and transition within the national leadership.",
